## Week 3 Priority-Aware Contention Sweep

**Test module:** `tests/test_p4_week3_priority.py`

**Benchmark script:** `scripts/p4_week3_contention.py`

**Capacity:** 15 agents per corridor across corridors 0, 1, and 2

**Method:** 10 seeds for each agent count, with snapshots at timestamps 0, 2, 4, 6, and 8 seconds.

| Agents (N) | Mean corridor 0 load | Mean corridor 1 load | Mean corridor 2 load | Mean overflow | Mean post-first changes | Emergency priority compliance |
|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| 30 | 10.00 | 10.00 | 10.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 1.00 |
| 45 | 15.00 | 15.00 | 15.00 | 0.00 | 0.00 | 1.00 |
| 60 | 20.00 | 20.00 | 20.00 | 15.00 | 0.00 | 1.00 |

The priority-aware policy processes agents in EMERGENCY, EVTOL, then DELIVERY order, with agent ID breaking ties within a priority. Existing assignments are retained while their corridor remains below capacity, limiting unnecessary movement. If no corridor has capacity, the least-loaded corridor receives the assignment and overflow is incremented. The sweep confirmed zero post-first-update corridor changes and complete EMERGENCY priority compliance.

